    "senderName": "NWS Peachtree City GA",
    "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued August 28 at 5:36PM EDT by NWS Peachtree City GA",
    "description": "At 536 PM EDT, a strong thunderstorm was over Whitesville-Pine Lake,\nor 8 miles west of Hamilton, moving southeast at 15 mph.\n\nHAZARD...40 to 50 mph wind, up to penny sized hail, frequent cloud\nto ground lightning and heavy rain.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Expect minor damage to tree limbs and blowing around of\nlight, unsecured objects. Heavy rain may cause temporary\nstreet flooding especially in poor drainage areas.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nHamilton, Jones Crossroads, Mountain Hill, and Whitesville-Pine Lake.",
    "instruction": "People outdoors should seek shelter immediately. If you can hear\nthunder, you are close enough to be struck by lightning. Motorists\nshould slow down and be prepared for possible loss of control due to\nhydroplaning.",
    "response": "Execute",
